From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:39:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 36/38] drm/imagination: Evict idle BOs under memory pressure

Idle clients keep every mapped BO unswappable on small-memory systems.
Use the GEM LRUs and shrinker to release native shmem backing while
preserving GPU virtual addresses. Require all mapping VMs to be idle,
with published retirement timestamps, for a one-second quiet period.

Trylock every VM under the BO reservation before editing any PTE. Mark
each cleared VA and vm_bo evicted, publish the MMU invalidation, then zap
CPU mappings, DMA-unmap and release the sole sgt page reference. Keep
pages on any partial unmap or flush failure for submit-time repair.

Never reclaim imports, exports (including export publication), kernel
BOs, PM/FW-protected BOs, vmaps, explicit pins or additional page users.
The Apple veto trylocks submit_lock and S8003 checks pm_last/pm_prev,
attached versus firmware gen, fault/booted, and each pm[].scene/td_seq
through s8003_pm_idle(). Track the last two geometry VM targets; no new
register access is introduced. T8010 keeps its generation invalidation.

Use base.gem_lru_mutex, required by drm_gem_lru, rather than a private LRU
lock. Reclaim edits use GFP_NOWAIT cursors. IMG KCCB flushing can acquire
power/CCB locks and reset firmware: schedule its scan in ordinary work
context rather than invoke it from direct reclaim. Eviction is enabled
on every device. Apple scans publish RAM-only tags directly in reclaim.

Expose controls and resident/evicted bytes, counters and skip reasons in
gem_evict; writing a MiB limit requests one pass. No swap, no eviction.

Affects: every PowerVR device

Assisted-by: LLM
